      "note": "getDescriptor(eSwitch, ...) answers nothing for either PoE switch; both are filed under eMultiLayerSwitch."
    },
    "pt_switch_module_support": {
      "3650-24PS": true,
      "3560-24PS": false,
      "2960-24TT": false,
      "note": "The catalog declares AC-POWER-SUPPLY and POWER-COVER-PLATE as module_type 4, which is ePtSwitchModule. The 3650-24PS root exposes three eNonRemovableModule slots against one on the 3560-24PS. This is consistent with the two empty supply bays seen in Physical view and with the 3650 boot line inline power denied, and it does NOT establish that installing a supply enables inline power. Only a governed observation could."
    },
    "interpretation_limit": "Factory structure only. No field here observes power delivery, installed hardware, or an administrative power state, and none of it promotes a capability or authorizes a PoE binding. A descriptor is not a runtime Module.",
    "access_point_consequence": "PT 9.0.1 defines eAccessPointPowerAdaptor, and the exact model AccessPoint-PT does not support it, while the exact endpoint model that already qualified positively, 7960, does support eIpPhonePowerAdapter. Every governed positive needs a differential against an endpoint whose external supply can be withheld, so this is the measured reason the AccessPoint-PT arms were unobservable. It is structural evidence, not a behavioural proof that no AccessPoint-PT can ever be powered."
  }
